// Repair and sale (WP6.6, docs/rules/repair_sell.md). Read by sf_data::repair; sf_bridge::repair_rules
// hands the numbers to the world (World::with_repair). All four are placeholders for the balance
// rounds of phase 15 and the playtest of M1; whole numbers only, no float and no tolerance anywhere.
(
    // Hit points a repairing structure gains per tick (1 to 1000). 1 per tick at 20 ticks a second
    // is 20 hit points a second: a power plant of 600 hit points is whole again in thirty seconds.
    // It was 3 until WP9.1e: the construction centre has no price, so its repair is free, and at 3 it
    // out-healed up to five idle light tanks for ever (six needed 6,052 ticks); at 1 four tanks take it
    // down in 1,131 ticks (measured, docs/rules/repair_sell.md "The rate and the wave").
    hp_per_tick: 1,
    // What a repair from nothing to full hit points costs, in thousandths of the structure's
    // price (0 to 1000). 250 means a quarter of the price for the whole of it; a repair of part of
    // the damage costs that part, rounded down on the running total, so the ticks add up to
    // exactly the cost of the gap. 0 makes repair free.
    full_cost_permille: 250,
    // Ticks a sale takes (1 to 6000). 100 is five seconds. The structure counts as gone from the
    // first tick and is removed when the time is up.
    sell_ticks: 100,
    // The part of the price paid back for a structure at full hit points, in thousandths (0 to
    // 1000). The refund is scaled by the hit points the structure has when the sale ends, rounded
    // down: price * refund_permille * hp / (max_hp * 1000).
    refund_permille: 500,
)
